00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.620
When it comes to this Fox versus Trump thing,
let me zoom out a little bit.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:11.470
Fox News and even corporate media more broadly,
our what we call sense-making tools and they

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:14.719
are terrible sense-making tools for society.

00:03:14.719 --> 00:03:20.370
So when we talk about sensemaking and media,
this is maybe one of the most important analyses

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:21.370
that we can do.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.370
And I get it.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:25.790
We're, we started with a Sharpie, but again,
I'm making an effort to really provide broader

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:29.999
and important contexts for when we do these
media analysis stories.

00:03:29.999 --> 00:03:35.889
When we talk about, uh, the sense-making analysis
for media, it goes well beyond the propaganda

00:03:35.889 --> 00:03:36.889
value of media.

00:03:36.889 --> 00:03:42.069
We've talked a lot about the propaganda value
of media and how media can sort of serve corporate

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:44.819
interests or political interests for one party
or another party.

00:03:44.819 --> 00:03:47.090
And you really have to zoom out to understand
this.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.949
We are an estimated on this planet.

00:03:48.949 --> 00:03:54.109
We are an estimated 7.7 billion people, each
kind of existing in our little corner of it

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:58.790
only having an awareness of a tiny, tiny fraction
each day of what happens on our planet.

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:03.489
A nearly infinite, I know that that's not
a precise term, nearly infinite, but I think

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:04.489
people know what I mean.

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:06.389
A nearly infinite number of things.

00:04:06.389 --> 00:04:09.939
It takes place every day depending on how
you measure them.

00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:16.750
Births, deaths, violence, storms, crimes,
entrepreneurship, food, growing medicine,

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:17.750
technology, right?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:22.009
I mean it's like the, the list doesn't do
it justice because think about everything

00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:25.590
that goes on in our planet in one day.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.550
Sense-Making is giving meaning to what goes
on in our world so that we can understand

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:35.550
it because again, so much happens every day
that the mind cannot actually comprehend it.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:40.520
So sense-making is giving meaning to, to things
that are going on and this is actually what

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.780
corporate media serves on a plate for us.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:47.199
We can't possibly follow every development
that takes place on our planet.

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:52.919
So what media does is not only do they explain
things to us, but they also narrow the scope

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:54.900
of what we pay attention to.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:05:00.580
And by virtue of that, they assign meaning
to what areas of life should we be paying

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.090
attention to.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:07.270
Local News, your 11:00 PM local news takes
everything that happened in the day and it

00:05:07.270 --> 00:05:12.270
makes sense of the world by picking, you know,
it's usually like five stories.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:15.910
One or two are usually about some horrible
crime that took place.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.750
They give you the weather and then a couple
of other stories and that's how they make

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.479
sense of the day.

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:22.479
For you.

00:05:22.479 --> 00:05:27.520
And as I've talked about countless times about
corporate media, there is really no one media

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:28.760
outlet including me.

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.460
I mean I'm including myself in this.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.129
There is no one media outlet that can really
do sense-making justice because there's just

00:05:35.129 --> 00:05:37.259
too much that happens in the world.

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:41.509
So to be an informed person, I've talked about
the knowledge pyramid before.

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:46.560
Oftentimes when I go in, I talk to uh, at
colleges and universities about critical thinking

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.560
and epistemology.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:50.650
The Knowledge Pyramid is this thing that you
have to build up.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:55.800
And the bottom of the pyramid is critical
thinking skills, epistemology skills, learning

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.610
how to think, learning how to learn.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.509
You then build the pyramid further by taking
those epistemological skills and you want

00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:11.530
to gain subject matter knowledge about sociology,
culture, physics, math, whatever, right?

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.870
You get subject matter knowledge.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:18.160
And then at the very top of the pyramid is
sort of like what happens day to day.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:24.500
You have to use that entire base of the pyramid
to interpret a specific event to solve a specific

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.500
math problem.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:30.569
For example, when you think about knowledge
this way, Fox News, calling Trump out or not

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:35.490
calling Trump out really doesn't make a big
difference in terms of foxes bigger picture

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.210
sense making capacity.

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:43.650
But when we think of the universe in which
your average Trumpist is operating, people

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:49.180
who don't have the epistemology and critical
thinking foundation, people who have not used

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:54.009
that foundation because they don't have it
to gain subject matter knowledge for them,

00:06:54.009 --> 00:06:55.860
their pyramid is truncated.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:01.900
And in those cases it actually can make a
difference that Fox News is saying the sharpie

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:03.900
image was completely bogus.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:09.539
It could pierce someone's echo chamber, it
could get someone to rethink their sense-making

00:07:09.539 --> 00:07:12.629
choices and it is still a good thing.

00:07:12.629 --> 00:07:14.290
That is a lot of context.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:20.139
But this is I think how we need to be thinking
about this very public sort of pseudo battle

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:25.590
between Donald Trump and fox news and Fox
News occasionally saying what you are saying

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.810
there isn't true.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:30.419
What Donald Trump said simply doesn't correspond
to the facts.

00:07:30.419 --> 00:07:33.710
And I think that if we want to be informed
news consumers and really be thinking about

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:38.449
these things more broadly, it's fun to watch
Shep Smith say Trump's a liar.

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:42.620
But we want to actually understand the context
and in the context for an audience that is

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:47.120
so lacking that critical thinking pyramid
and the subject matter knowledge, it could

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.590
actually get them to say, you know what, maybe
this guy is a liar and I shouldn't support

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:51.720
them in 2020

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.389
and to that extent, I think it's great.

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:58.240
Let's just not pretend that Fox News is not
still 95% carrying water for Donald Trump

